==Battleground==
*1 [[Mooth]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[Spiritual Yulala (Enemy)|Spiritual Yulala]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*3 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Kang Roo]] spawns as the boss after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Kang Roo]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Masked Grandmaster Cat (Enemy)|Masked Grandmaster Cat]] spawns after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 140 seconds<sup>4,200f</sup>, delay 50~53.33 seconds<sup>1,500f~1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is an endurance battle mostly similar to its [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 49|Heavenly Tower equivalent]], just with stronger Relic-traited bosses and [[Aku Gory]]'s occasional intervention. Anti-Relic specialists will come in handy as they could delay the bosses, giving others much more time to do damage and eventually remove them.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]] - A midranged tank with resistance to Relics and immunity to Warp and Curse, it can easily hold its ground against the main threats for some time while also doing decent damage as long as Aku Gory isn't around.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] - Doron performs incredibly well due to his massive combination of immunities and ability to knockback/Freeze Relic threats. His Omni Strike and extreme health ensure he'll easily get the hit off and regain lots of ground.
*[[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Maize]] - Maize can consistently stall Aku Gory for quite a while because it resists both Relic and Aku enemies. Its high speed also allows it to quickly recover from Yulala's Warp, and with immunity to Curse, the two main threats will have a hard time getting past.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone]]/[[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion]] - Hermit doesn't actually spawn until a bit later, so Manic Lion could be of some use in forcing Yulala to attack, while Stone is a great universal meatshield whose massive health and Warp Immunity allows it to simply block any of the threats during its very short lifetime.
*[[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] - Cossack cat's true form, Royal Guard Cat, is able to deal massive damage to both relic bosses. With the correct set-ups from the likes of Doron or the Thunderbolt cannon, this spammable unit can help tag on additional chip damage alongside your rushers. The true form also gains wave immunity, letting it ignore Masked Grandmaster's wave attacks. This can allow Royal Guard to act as an additional meatshield with the appropriate research UP combos, as he can tank both a Yulala or Grandmaster hit at Lv.39, albeit a very expensive one. Be wary of its significant weakness to the Aku Gorys though, as they will practically ignore the fella.
*[[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]] - Luza's Massive Damage/Resistance to Relics and Immunity to Warp/Curse allows it to deal quite a bit of damage while not faltering to Yulala's Warp, although it does require some support to make sure Aku Gory doesn't get to it.
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] - Being strong against Relics with a 4-second weaken as well as Curse and Wave Immunity, Naala is able to cripple the main threats if it gets a hit on them through her expansive LD attacks. Its weaknesses against other enemies still apply, and it may have to be deployed later as Yulala's 400-range Omni Strike can easily warp it.
*[[Ancient Egg: N006 (Special Cat)|Fallen BearCat]]: Despite it looking like they wouldn't get through the frontline hell of Yulala and Hermit's attacks, Fallen BearCat can land hits on Aku Gory very consistently, removing a massive stressor from this stage. They can get through if Hermit misses an attack, but the plentiful cash in this stage allows them to be spammed for occasional hits nonetheless.

===Recommended Ubers===
*Talented [[Gravi (Uber Rare Cat)|Gravolodon]] - With Target Relic and Curse Immunity unlocked, Gravolodon can be a surprisingly powerful tank, as its Wave/Warp Immunity can dismiss the bosses' abilities while its own Wave Attacks yield chip damage on them over time. Gravolodon should still be backed by units that can eliminate Aku Gories, as it has no way of getting them off it.
*[[Hades the Punisher (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Hades]] - Good usage here because of his warp immunity against Yulala and his insane health, making him a competent tank. However, he should be backed up by units that can kill Aku Gories quickly because they can shred him quite quickly.

